
# 9. Quick Sort

## Question Description
Implement the Quick Sort algorithm in C++ to sort an array in ascending order. Quick Sort uses the divide-and-conquer technique by selecting a pivot element and partitioning the array around it.

## Test Cases

### Test Case 1
Input: `[10, 7, 8, 9, 1, 5]`

Expected Output:
`[1, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10]`

### Test Case 2
Input: `[4, 2, 6, 1, 3]`

Expected Output:
`[1, 2, 3, 4, 6]`

### Test Case 3
Input: `[5, 5, 2, 1]`

Expected Output:
`[1, 2, 5, 5]`

## Time Complexity
- Best Case: O(n log n)
- Average Case: O(n log n)
- Worst Case: O(n²)

## Space Complexity
- Average: O(log n) auxiliary stack space
- Worst Case: O(n) auxiliary stack space
